      content:
          'A 28-year-old female is referred to the burn rehabilitation clinic 4 months after sustaining severe facial, neck, and bilateral hand burns from a deliberate acid attack by a former partner. She underwent emergent irrigation and debridement in the ED, followed by three staged reconstructive surgeries including split-thickness skin grafting to her bilateral hands and neck, and a full-thickness skin graft from her groin to her left cheek. Additional reconstructive procedures are planned, including nasal reconstruction and revision of oral commissure contracture. She has not left her parents\' home since hospital discharge 2 months ago. She wears a scarf covering her entire face when anyone other than her parents is present, including during this clinic visit. Her mother accompanies her and reports the patient has been sleeping 16 hours per day, eating very little, and has made statements about \'not wanting to be here anymore.\'',
