    Section(
      title: 'History & Systems Review:',
      content:
          '- **Injury Details**: Deliberate acid attack (concentrated sulfuric acid) by ex-boyfriend 4 months ago. Burns to face (forehead spared by hairline, full-thickness burns to bilateral cheeks, nose, lips, chin), anterior neck (circumferential deep partial to full-thickness), and bilateral dorsal hands (deep partial-thickness — defensive injuries).\n- **Surgical History**: (1) ED irrigation and debridement day 0; (2) STSG bilateral dorsal hands and anterior neck, day 7; (3) FTSG from left groin to left cheek, day 21; (4) Oral commissure release and Z-plasty, day 45. Planned: nasal reconstruction with paramedian forehead flap, right cheek revision, eyelid reconstruction.\n- **Current Wound Status**: All grafts healed. Active hypertrophic scarring throughout. Developing microstomia (oral aperture 25 mm, premorbid estimated 45-50 mm). Left nasal alar collapse with partial nasal airway obstruction. Right lower eyelid ectropion requiring taping.\n- **Functional Impact**: Cannot open mouth wide enough to eat solid foods — on soft/puree diet. Difficulty with oral hygiene. Cannot apply makeup (previously important to her). Bilateral hand scarring limits fine motor — cannot button clothes or open containers independently.\n- **Pain**: Neuropathic burning in facial scars 7/10. Severe pruritus of neck and hand scars. Currently on gabapentin 600 mg TID and oxycodone 10 mg Q6H PRN.\n- **Psychological**: PHQ-9 score 24 (severe depression). PTSD Checklist (PCL-5) score 62 (clinical PTSD; cutoff 33). Reports nightmares 4-5 nights/week of the attack. Hypervigilance — startles at loud noises, cannot be in same room as men other than her father. Suicidal ideation — passive ("I don\'t want to be here") without active plan. Refusing psychiatric medication — "pills won\'t fix my face."\n- **Social**: Single. Previously worked as a dental hygienist — cannot return due to facial scarring and hand dysfunction. Living with parents. No income. Has not spoken to friends since the attack. Victim protection order in place against the attacker, who is incarcerated awaiting trial.\n- **PMH**: Previously healthy. No prior psychiatric history.\n- **Medications**: Gabapentin 600 mg TID, oxycodone 10 mg Q6H PRN, diphenhydramine 25 mg PRN pruritus, melatonin 5 mg QHS',
