          '**Vitals**: BP 110/68 mmHg, HR 76 bpm, RR 14, SpO2 99% on RA, Temp 36.7C, BMI 19.2 (pre-injury BMI 23).\n\n**General**: Thin female wearing a full-face scarf. Reluctantly removes scarf after reassurance. Avoids eye contact. Flat affect. Whispered responses.\n\n**Face and Neck**:\n- **Forehead**: Spared above hairline. Mild scarring at hairline border.\n- **Bilateral cheeks**: Full-thickness grafted areas with raised, erythematous, firm hypertrophic scars. Left cheek FTSG is a different color and texture than surrounding skin. Right cheek has contracted, irregular scar tissue pending revision.\n- **Nose**: Significant alar destruction bilaterally. Left nostril collapsed. Breathing through mouth primarily. Nasal reconstruction planned.\n- **Lips**: Scarring of both lips with loss of vermillion border definition. **Oral commissure contracture** — microstomia with oral aperture measuring **25 mm** (functional minimum for eating is approximately 35-40 mm). Z-plasty sites healing but contracture recurrence beginning.\n- **Eyelids**: Right lower eyelid ectropion — scleral show 3 mm, incomplete eye closure with forced blink. Taping in place. Left eyelids intact but with scar banding inferiorly.\n- **Neck**: Circumferential hypertrophic scarring. Band-like anterior scar contracture limiting neck extension to 10 degrees (normal 45-60). Chin-to-chest distance limited.\n- **Ears**: Right ear — loss of superior helix from acid exposure. Left ear intact.\n\n**Bilateral Hands**:\n- **Dorsal surface**: Grafted, healed. Active hypertrophic scarring with web space contracture between thumb and index finger bilaterally. First web space angle 25 degrees (normal 45-60 degrees).\n- **ROM**: MCP flexion 60/80 degrees (limited by dorsal scar tightness). Grip strength R 10 kg, L 8 kg (severely reduced; pre-injury estimated 25-30 kg). Fine motor: unable to pick up a penny, difficulty with buttons, cannot hold a toothbrush effectively.\n- **Sensation**: Hypersensitivity of grafted areas. Pain with light touch over dorsal hands.\n\n**Psychological Observation**: Does not initiate conversation. Answers in 1-2 word whispers. Becomes tearful when scarf is removed. Flinches when the (male) medical assistant enters the room. Mother provides most of the history.',
